 ['DictReader on the file with a header row, and with made-up names', 'import csv, os, tempfile\nos.chdir(tempfile.mkdtemp())\nrows = "4/5/2035 13:34,Apples,73\\n4/5/2035 3:41,Cherries,85\\n4/6/2035 12:46,Pears,14\\n4/8/2035 8:59,Oranges,52\\n4/10/2035 2:07,Apples,152\\n4/10/2035 18:10,Bananas,23\\n4/10/2035 2:40,Strawberries,98\\n"\nopen(\'exampleWithHeader3.csv\', \'w\').write(\'Timestamp,Fruit,Quantity\\n\' + rows)\nopen(\'example3.csv\', \'w\').write(rows)\nexample_file = open(\'exampleWithHeader3.csv\')\ndata = list(csv.DictReader(example_file))\nprint(len(data), data[0])\nexample_file = open(\'exampleWithHeader3.csv\')\nfor row in csv.DictReader(example_file):\n    print(row[\'Timestamp\'], row[\'Fruit\'], row[\'Quantity\'])\nexample_file = open(\'example3.csv\')\nprint(list(csv.DictReader(example_file))[0])\nexample_file = open(\'example3.csv\')\nfor row in csv.DictReader(example_file, [\'time\', \'name\', \'amount\']):\n    print(row[\'time\'], row[\'name\'], row[\'amount\'])', "7 {'Timestamp': '4/5/2035 13:34', 'Fruit': 'Apples', 'Quantity': '73'}\n4/5/2035 13:34 Apples 73\n4/5/2035 3:41 Cherries 85\n4/6/2035 12:46 Pears 14\n4/8/2035 8:59 Oranges 52\n4/10/2035 2:07 Apples 152\n4/10/2035 18:10 Bananas 23\n4/10/2035 2:40 Strawberries 98\n{'4/5/2035 13:34': '4/5/2035 3:41', 'Apples': 'Cherries', '73': '85'}\n4/5/2035 13:34 Apples 73\n4/5/2035 3:41 Cherries 85\n4/6/2035 12:46 Pears 14\n4/8/2035 8:59 Oranges 52\n4/10/2035 2:07 Apples 152\n4/10/2035 18:10 Bananas 23\n4/10/2035 2:40 Strawberries 98"],
