 ['what dumps refuses, what it changes, and the 3.14 notes', "import json, datetime\nfor v in ({1, 2}, datetime.date(2035, 4, 5), open):\n    try:\n        json.dumps(v)\n    except TypeError as e:\n        print(e)\nprint(json.loads(json.dumps({'t': (1, 2), 'k': {1: 'a'}})))\ntry:\n    json.dumps({'k': [{'a': {1, 2}}]})\nexcept TypeError as e:\n    print(e, e.__notes__)", 'Object of type set is not JSON serializable\nObject of type date is not JSON serializable\nObject of type builtin_function_or_method is not JSON serializable\n{\'t\': [1, 2], \'k\': {\'1\': \'a\'}}\nObject of type set is not JSON serializable ["when serializing dict item \'a\'", \'when serializing list item 0\', "when serializing dict item \'k\'"]'],
